Build succeeds. The only warning is the expected `sorry` for the unproved conjecture.

**Summary of `conjectures/42.lean`:**

- **`IsSidonSet`** — A finite set where all pairwise sums are distinct (B₂ set)
- **`DisjointDifferences`** — Two sets whose difference sets intersect only at {0}
- **`erdos_problem_42`** — For every M ≥ 1, there exists N₀ such that for all N ≥ N₀, every Sidon set A ⊆ {1,…,N} admits another Sidon set B ⊆ {1,…,N} of size M with (A−A) ∩ (B−B) = {0}
